================================================================================

PROJECT CSS STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

my-react-app/
│
├── src/
│   │
│   ├── components/
│   │   │
│   │   ├── Header/
│   │   │   ├── Header.jsx
│   │   │   └── Header.css
│   │   │
│   │   ├── Footer/
│   │   │   ├── Footer.jsx
│   │   │   └── Footer.css
│   │   │
│   │   ├── Button/
│   │   │   ├── Button.jsx
│   │   │   └── Button.css
│   │   │
│   │   └── Card/
│   │       ├── Card.jsx
│   │       └── Card.css
│   │
│   ├── App.jsx
│   ├── App.css
│   ├── main.jsx
│   └── index.css
│
└── index.html


CSS FILE ORGANIZATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+-------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
| FILE                                | PURPOSE                                |
+-------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
| src/index.css                       | Global/base styles                     |
|                                     | Reset/normalize                       |
|                                     | Global variables                      |
|                                     | Typography                            |
| src/App.css                         | Application-level layout              |
|                                     | Main containers                       |
| src/components/Header/Header.css    | Header-specific styling               |
| src/components/Footer/Footer.css    | Footer-specific styling               |
| src/components/Button/Button.css    | Button component styling              |
| src/components/Card/Card.css        | Card component styling                |
+-------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+


CSS ORGANIZATION PRINCIPLES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Global CSS
  - Shared/global styles belong in index.css

• Component CSS
  - Component-related styles stay near the component

• Clear Naming
  - Class names should communicate their purpose

• Avoid Conflicts
  - Use component-oriented naming conventions

• Reusable Patterns
  - Share genuinely reusable tokens/utilities

• Separation of Concerns
  - Keep component implementation and styles organized

• Single Responsibility
  - Each CSS file should have a clear purpose

• Avoid Unnecessary Duplication
  - Reuse variables and shared patterns

• Maintainability
  - Styles should be easy to locate and change

• Remove Unused CSS
  - Avoid carrying unnecessary rules


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Importing a normal .css file from a React component does NOT automatically
scope those CSS selectors to that component.

Normal CSS remains global after it is included in the application's CSS
bundle/style graph.

Example:

import './Card.css'

does NOT make:

.card { ... }

technically private to Card.jsx.

Component-specific naming conventions or CSS Modules can prevent accidental
selector collisions more reliably.


