================================================================================
PART 5: CSS NAMING CONVENTIONS
================================================================================

BEM - BLOCK ELEMENT MODIFIER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BEM is a CSS naming methodology.

BEM means:

B = Block
E = Element
M = Modifier


BLOCK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Standalone component:

.card { }


ELEMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Part of the block:

.card__title { }

.card__description { }

.card__footer { }


MODIFIER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Variation/state:

.card--featured { }

.card--small { }

.card--large { }


ELEMENT MODIFIER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.card__title--highlight { }

.card__button--disabled { }


BEM TABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| PATTERN                  | EXAMPLE                                    |
+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| Block                    | .card                                      |
| Block__Element           | .card__title                               |
|                          | .card__description                         |
| Block--Modifier          | .card--featured                            |
|                          | .card--small                               |
| Block__Element--Modifier | .card__title--highlight                    |
|                          | .card__button--disabled                    |
+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


IMPORTANT BEM CORRECTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For a modifier applied to an element, use:

.card__button--disabled


For a modifier applied to the block:

.card--featured


A class such as:

.card--featured__title

is not the usual BEM structure.

A more typical combination is:

<div className="card card--featured">

  <h2 className="card__title">
    ...
  </h2>

</div>


================================================================================
NAMING BEST PRACTICES
================================================================================

• Use meaningful names

• Prefer names describing purpose/role

• Stay consistent

• Avoid unnecessary abbreviations

• Use one naming convention consistently

• Use BEM when it helps manage larger CSS structures

• Avoid highly generic names when collisions are likely


GOOD VS BAD NAMING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| ISSUE                | LESS CLEAR           | CLEARER                    |
+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| Generic              | .box                 | .product-card              |
| Unclear              | .item-1              | .navigation-item           |
| Abbreviation         | .btn-prim            | .button-primary            |
| BEM inconsistency    | .card_title          | .card__title               |
| Generic state        | .active              | .navigation__item--active  |
| Appearance-driven    | .blue-button         | .button--primary           |
| Vague modifier       | .card-new            | .card--featured            |
+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+


