PART 8: RESPONSIVE DESIGN WITH CSS
================================================================================

RESPONSIVE DESIGN PRINCIPLES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Responsive design includes:

• Flexible Layouts

• Flexbox

• CSS Grid

• Relative sizing

• Media queries

• Appropriate breakpoints

• Responsive typography

• Touch-friendly controls


================================================================================
COMMON BREAKPOINT EXAMPLES
================================================================================

These are example project breakpoints, NOT universal device standards.

+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| RANGE / TARGET          | EXAMPLE                                   |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| Small screens           | Up to ~480px                              |
| Medium screens          | Around 768px                              |
| Desktop layout change   | Around 1024px                             |
| Wide layout change      | Around 1440px                             |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


Choose breakpoints based on where YOUR layout needs to change rather than
trying to target every specific device model.


================================================================================
MOBILE-FIRST RESPONSIVE EXAMPLE
================================================================================

/* Base: Small screens */

.card-grid {
  display: grid;

  grid-template-columns:
    1fr;

  gap:
    var(--spacing-md);
}


.card {
  padding:
    var(--spacing-md);
}


.card-title {
  font-size:
    var(--font-size-base);
}


/* Tablet / Medium */

@media (min-width: 768px) {

  .card-grid {

    grid-template-columns:
      repeat(2, 1fr);

  }


  .card {
    padding:
      var(--spacing-lg);
  }


  .card-title {
    font-size:
      var(--font-size-large);
  }

}


/* Desktop */

@media (min-width: 1024px) {

  .card-grid {

    grid-template-columns:
      repeat(3, 1fr);

  }


  .card {
    padding:
      var(--spacing-xl);
  }


  .card-title {
    font-size:
      var(--font-size-xl);
  }

}


/* Wide Desktop */

@media (min-width: 1440px) {

  .card-grid {

    grid-template-columns:
      repeat(4, 1fr);

  }

}


RESPONSIVE TECHNIQUES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+-----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+
| TECHNIQUE             | PURPOSE                  | EXAMPLE                     |
+-----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+
| Flexbox               | Flexible 1D layouts      | display: flex               |
| CSS Grid              | Grid/2D layouts          | display: grid               |
| Media Queries         | Conditional CSS          | @media (...)                |
| Percentage Width      | Relative sizing          | width: 100%                 |
| max-width             | Limit content size       | max-width: 1200px           |
| Viewport Units        | Viewport-relative sizing | 100vw, 100vh                |
| clamp()               | Fluid constrained values | clamp(...)                  |
| Mobile First          | Start small              | Base + min-width queries    |
+-----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+


================================================================================
FLUID TYPOGRAPHY EXAMPLE
================================================================================

.title {

  font-size:
    clamp(
      1.5rem,
      4vw,
      3rem
    );

}


Meaning:

Minimum:
1.5rem

Preferred responsive value:
4vw

Maximum:
3rem


